infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Routing match cost: linear scan vs radix trie
  desc Both are microseconds — but only one stays flat as the route table grows
  compares
    - label Linear scan
      children
        - label O(n) in route count
          desc Match time grows with every route you register
        - label Tries each route in order
          desc Dead simple; fine for dozens of routes
        - label Degrades as routes pile up
          desc 10,000 routes can mean 10,000 checks in the worst case
        - label No prefix sharing
          desc Each pattern is compared independently
    - label Radix trie
      children
        - label O(path length)
          desc Cost tracks the URL, not the size of the route table
        - label Independent of route count
          desc 10 routes and 10,000 routes match in the same time
        - label Prefix tree over path segments
          desc Shared prefixes collapse into a single walk
        - label httprouter, Echo, Fastify use it
          desc The standard once the route table gets large
theme
  palette #f59e0b #14b8a6
